# MCSP Self-Scaffolding 0.36

Status: Constructive self-description experiment
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Parent lineage: 0.31 normal form, 0.26 propagation, 0.25 structural scaffold

## Objective

Determine whether an MCSP scaffold can carry and qualify the structural obligations needed to propagate a successor scaffold without documentary names deciding semantic equivalence.

This checkpoint does not claim semantic closure.

## Structural role pre-settlement

The experiment pre-settles a finite structural vocabulary using numeric bootstrap identities:

    0x01 material invariant
    0x02 applicability
    0x03 dimension status
    0x04 qualification
    0x05 unresolved residue
    0x06 lineage parent
    0x07 lineage child
    0x08 propagation event

These numbers are bootstrap representation tokens. Their numeric values are not universal semantic identities.

The material commitment is the qualified relation among the roles, not their English documentary names.

## Self-scaffold record

A self-scaffold is projected as ordered role/value pairs:

    role,value

The role sequence is itself carried by the scaffold fixture rather than inferred from source variable names.

A successor qualifies only if:

1. every required structural role remains present;
2. material invariant remains compatible;
3. applicability is inherited unless an explicit qualified narrowing event exists;
4. OPEN remains OPEN unless an explicit qualified settlement event exists;
5. unresolved residue is not silently discarded;
6. failed qualification does not propagate;
7. lineage identifies the declared parent and successor;
8. normalization produces the declared structural fingerprint.

## Name independence

Documentary names, comments, assembler labels and source symbol spelling SHALL NOT participate in the normalized projection.

Renaming documentary source labels while retaining role/value structure must not change the projection.

## Self-propagation boundary

The experiment is self-scaffolding because the structural roles required to judge propagation are represented inside the scaffold being processed.

It is not yet full self-description because:
- the evaluator procedure is still authored externally in assembly;
- bootstrap numeric role tokens are admitted;
- interpretation of the initial role contract is pre-settled by this version;
- the kernel is not yet encoded wholly by MCSP-native structures.

## Adversarial cases

S1 compatible successor: PASS expected.
S2 material invariant mutation: FAIL expected.
S3 residue loss: FAIL expected.
S4 applicability narrowing without event: FAIL expected.
S5 applicability narrowing with qualified event: PASS expected.
S6 OPEN->PRESET without settlement event: FAIL expected.
S7 OPEN->PRESET with qualified settlement event: PASS expected.
S8 failed successor qualification: FAIL expected.
S9 documentary-label independence: structural projection unchanged.
S10 deterministic reconstruction: repeated normalization identical.

Kernel remains DETERMINATE CONDITION.
